body.zh-TW:
在終端機授權 Claude 修改專案時，若沒有特別劃定邊界，工具可能會不小心碰到其他資料夾。現在新增了 `permissions.blockWritesOutsideWorkingDirectories` 設定。只要在設定檔中啟用，無論目前處於哪種權限模式，Write、Edit 與 NotebookEdit 等所有寫入工具，都會直接拒絕修改工作目錄外的路徑。

```json
{
  "permissions": {
    "blockWritesOutsideWorkingDirectories": true
  }
}
```

⟦猶如在木工工作台上加裝安全擋板，以前工具運轉時容易削到桌緣外的雜物，現在所有切削刀具都被硬性限制在桌面範圍內。⟧當你要讓工具自動修改大量檔案時，開啟這項設定就能確保專案以外的個人檔案不會被意外改動。

body.en:
When authorizing Claude to modify a project in the terminal, tools might accidentally touch other folders if boundaries are not specifically defined. A new `permissions.blockWritesOutsideWorkingDirectories` setting has now been added. Once enabled in the configuration file, all writing tools such as Write, Edit, and NotebookEdit will directly refuse to modify paths outside the working directories, regardless of the current permission mode.

```json
{
  "permissions": {
    "blockWritesOutsideWorkingDirectories": true
  }
}
```

⟦Picture a safety guard mounted on a woodworking workbench: operating tools previously risked shaving clutter beyond the table edge, but now every cutting blade is strictly confined within the tabletop.⟧ When letting tools automatically modify large numbers of files, enabling this setting ensures personal files outside the project are not accidentally changed.
